\ncompiled_flatbuffer = compile_str(CODE, target_backends=[\"dylib\"], input_type=\"mhlo\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nGet:\r\n```\r\n$ python q.py\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/phawkins/jax/q.py\", line 25, in <module>\r\n    compiled_flatbuffer = compile_str(CODE, target_backends=[\"dylib\"], input_type=\"mhlo\")\r\n  File \"/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py39/lib/python3.9/site-packages/iree/compiler/tools/core.py\", line 262, in compile_str\r\n    result = invoke_immediate(cl, immediate_input=input_bytes)\r\n  File \"/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py39/lib/python3.9/site-packages/iree/compiler/tools/binaries.py\", line 201, in invoke_immediate\r\n    raise CompilerToolError(process)\r\niree.compiler.tools.binaries.CompilerToolError: Error invoking IREE compiler tool ireec\r\nDiagnostics:\r\n<stdin>:4:12: error: 'std.call' op operand type mismatch: expected operand type '!hal.buffer_view', but provided 'tensor<f32>' for operand number 0\r\n    %0:2 = call @\"jit_jvp(f)\"(%arg0) : (tensor<f32>) -> (tensor<f32>, tensor<f32>)\r\n           ^\r\n<stdin>:2:1: error: conversion from source -> vm failed\r\nmodule  {\r\n^\r\n\r\n\r\nInvoked with:\r\n ireec /home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py39/lib/python3.9/site-packages/iree/compiler/tools/../_mlir_libs/ireec - --iree-input-type=mhlo --iree-vm-bytecode-module-output-format=flatbuffer-binary --iree-hal-target-backends=dylib --iree-mlir-to-vm-bytecode-module --iree-llvm-embedded-linker-path=/home/phawkins/.pyenv/versions/py39/lib/python3.9/site-packages/iree/compiler/tools/../_mlir_libs/iree-lld --mlir-print-debuginfo --mlir-print-op-on-diagnostic=false\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe IR looks legal to me, but perhaps I'm missing something.","closed_at":"2022-06-13T18:57:25Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309732?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co